<title>KAZAKHSTAN: Kazakh Feb oil output falls mth/mth to 1.897 mln T.</title>
<headline>Kazakh Feb oil output falls mth/mth to 1.897 mln T.</headline>
<dateline>ALMATY 1997-03-18</dateline>
<text>
<p>Kazakhstan produced 1.897 million tonnes of crude oil and gas condensate in February, down 10 percent from January output of 2.113 million tonnes, the State Statistics Committee said on Tuesday.</p>
<p>The committee released the following figures for energy output in its latest monthly statistical bulletin. Figures in tonnes, except crude oil in million tonnes and natural gas in billion cubic meters.</p>
<p> KAZAKH ENERGY OUTPUT	Feb 97	 Jan 97	Jan-Feb 97</p>
<p> Crude oil			1.897	  2.113	   4.010</p>
<p>  mth/mth pct change	-10.2	   -1.2	     n/a</p>
<p>  yr/yr   pct change	+12.2	  +17.4	   +14.9</p>
<p> Natural gas		    0.61	   0.68	    1.3</p>
<p>  mth/mth pct change	-10.1	   +3.3	     n/a</p>
<p>  yr/yr   pct change	+19.1	  +18.3	   +18.7</p>
<p> Gasoline		    122,700	106,600	  229,300</p>
<p>  mth/mth pct change	+15.1	  -25.2	     n/a</p>
<p>  yr/yr   pct change	-37.0	  -45.2	   -41.1</p>
<p> Diesel			185,400	195,900	  381,300</p>
<p>  mth/mth pct change	 -5.4	   -6.3	     n/a</p>
<p>  yr/yr   pct change	 +3.3	  -17.6	    -8.6</p>
<p> Fuel oil		    285,700	344,200	  629,900</p>
<p>  mth/mth pct change	-17.0	   +4.2	     n/a</p>
<p>  yr/yr   pct change	-20.4	   +6.7	    -7.6</p>
<p>-- Almaty Newsroom +7 3272 509410</p>
</text>
